  "schema_version": "formalization-faithfulness-1",
  "role": "adjudicator",
  "task_id": "LEV-CH01-ACOUSTICS-RIGHT-MODE-ALGEBRAIC-PRODUCTION-20260908",
  "trigger": [
    "judge classifications differ",
    "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
    "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
    "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D001 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The difference results from incomplete structure evidence in the blind dossier. The supplied complete local source establishes the missing characterization, supporting faithful-equivalent rather than undetermined.",
      "primary_evidence": "The inline LinearAcoustics.lean source explicitly declares structure LinearAcousticsSolution with density_ne_zero, pressure, velocity, and satisfies fields. The attached printed page 2 derives the selected mode equation from the same acoustic equations."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The requested characterization is established: every system carries the acoustic equations for its own pressure and velocity projections at every real point. This follows from the structure declaration, without relying on a constructor name or majority agreement.",
      "primary_evidence": "The complete structure declaration includes satisfies : ∀ x t, IsLinearAcousticsSolutionAt pressure velocity bulkModulus density x t."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "The round-trip judgment appropriately preserved uncertainty given its evidence. The additional complete declaration supplied to this adjudication removes that uncertainty; both implication directions hold.",
      "primary_evidence": "The round-trip finding concerns only recovery of the input PDE assumptions. The complete LinearAcousticsSolution structure exposes those assumptions as a field, and D004–D006 expose the exact constructed-field PDE conclusion."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D001 unclear",
      "resolution": "D001 is a structure with exactly the four displayed fields. Lean structures have a single constructor and projections recovering their fields. D007 describes its constructor, and D002–D003 recover its pressure and velocity fields. The bundle is neither an opaque unrestricted type nor a type with additional unexamined constructors.",
      "primary_evidence": "The complete inline source uses structure LinearAcousticsSolution (bulkModulus density : ℝ) where, followed by density_ne_zero, pressure, velocity, and satisfies. This declaration supplies the information absent from the blind inventory's Real → Real → Type entry."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "C02 passes. The system binder packages two real-valued fields on real space-time and their acoustic equations; it introduces no additional mathematical object restriction beyond the displayed fields.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 1 specifies real space-time and real-valued components; printed page 2 identifies the two components as p and u. The complete structure and D002–D003 give pressure velocity : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "C04 passes. Every system supplies all four actual partial derivatives and both acoustic equations everywhere. Positive K/rho expresses the inherited positive square-root speed condition. Nonzero density is already forced by positive ratio, so its bundled occurrence does not reduce applicability.",
      "primary_evidence": "The structure's satisfies field invokes D008, whose body requires four HasDerivAt certificates and pt + K*ux = 0 and ut + rho⁻¹*px = 0. Printed pages 1–2 give the derivative convention, equations (1.5), c = sqrt(K/rho), and c > 0."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "C06 passes. The complete structure resolves the outstanding local definition. Rechecking the reused declarations confirms actual acoustic derivatives, ordinary real multiplication and reciprocal, nonzero density, and the ordinary real scalar action and topology. Their current effects agree with the source; reuse hashes alone are not the basis of this conclusion.",
      "primary_evidence": "D008 explicitly links derivative witnesses to pressure and velocity slices. D010 supplies continuity of real multiplication, not regularity of those fields. D024 and D031 select real products; D051 is negated equality; D076 and D084 select real inversion; D094 defines scalar action by multiplication. D004–D006 and D049 give actual derivatives of p + rho*c*u and their transport equation."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "N06 passes. The structure supplies the needed input derivative existence for every system. The conclusion supplies derivative existence for the transformed field. No continuity of derivatives, additional existence theorem, or uniqueness assumption is imposed.",
      "primary_evidence": "The structure's satisfies field and D008 require pointwise slice derivatives. D006 requires the two slice derivatives of the mode. The selected source uses classical partial derivatives but states no named regularity class or existence-and-uniqueness result."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "The implication is yes. For any quantified system, its satisfies field gives precisely the source acoustic premises. With the prescribed positive square-root speed, the source conclusion becomes D006 for the exact D005 field at every point, and hence yields the translated conjunction.",
      "primary_evidence": "The full structure supplies the previously missing elimination information. Printed page 2 defines w^1 = p + rho*c*u with c = sqrt(K/rho) and asserts w^1_t + c*w^1_x = 0. D004 is an abbreviation for D006 with those identical arguments."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity, parameter scope, and purported strength",
      "resolution": "The claim is nonvacuous: K = rho = 1 and p(x,t) = u(x,t) = x-t satisfy every bundled premise and yield the nonconstant mode 2(x-t). Positive ratio excludes zero density and nonpositive radicands. Allowing both-negative parameters does not warrant faithful-stronger: the printed mathematical condition concerns the positive ratio, and even under a physical-positive reading negative pairs reduce to positive pairs by K' = -K, rho' = -rho, p' = p, u' = -u, preserving the ratio, acoustic equations, and constructed mode.",
      "primary_evidence": "D007 and the full structure impose only nonzero density and D008 everywhere; direct substitution gives pt = ut = -1 and px = ux = 1 for the positive example. D008 and D005 also directly verify the stated simultaneous sign transformation. Printed page 2 gives positive c and its square-root definition but no separate parameter inequalities."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "In the inherited global real-space-time classical setting, source acoustic fields and their derivatives can be packaged using the displayed structure constructor. The source's prescribed positive square-root speed gives K/rho > 0 and nonzero density. Applying the Lean proposition and unfolding D005, D004, and D006 yields actual partial derivatives of precisely w^1 = p + rho*c*u satisfying w^1_t + c*w^1_x = 0, together with positive c. The neighboring left-mode equation is outside the selected claim."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Every quantified system supplies its pressure and velocity fields and their acoustic equations through the complete structure's satisfies projection. Positive ratio gives the prescribed positive real square-root speed. The source assertion then yields the transport equation and classical derivative witnesses required by D006 for D005 at every real point. The positivity conjunct follows from the same ratio condition. If physical positivity of individual material parameters is additionally understood, both-negative target parameters reduce to positive parameters by simultaneously negating K, rho, and u while preserving p; this leaves the ratio and right-mode field unchanged."
    }
  },
  "classification": "faithful-equivalent",
  "accepted": true,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "blind-dossier-structure-omission",
      "evidence": "The blind dossier supplies D001's type and D007's constructor but omits the full structure declaration. The complete inline direct dossier explicitly supplies all four structure fields.",
      "impact": "The blind and round-trip uncertainty was an evidence limitation, not a demonstrated semantic mismatch. The complete declaration resolves it."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "classical-source-interpretation",
      "evidence": "The attached printed pages use real space-time, actual partial derivatives, constant material coefficients, and positive sound speed. D008 and D006 encode these derivative assertions pointwise without requiring continuous derivatives.",
      "impact": "Acceptance concerns the selected classical right-mode PDE. It does not assert physical realizability of negative material parameters or add claims about weak solutions, boundary conditions, or the separate left-moving mode."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Independent inspection of the attached source pages and the inline declaration evidence confirms the same fields, coefficients, square-root speed, signs, and actual partial derivatives. The complete structure declaration resolves every mechanically triggered uncertainty about arbitrary system inhabitants. Both implications hold through packaging and projection of the same acoustic premises, and an explicit nonconstant solution establishes nonvacuity. No target proof or external material was needed. Source-byte and rendering-hash verification are attributed to the orchestrator and were not independently recomputed."
}
